! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262 ("TEST EX AND EXIC"), TEST 1CC --
! "-TEST 1CC, CHK EX OF BRANCH AND EXE." -- the BE/BD/BB half, PDF
! pp.93-94, octal 023474.40-023545.40.  81 SOURCE ROWS over 83
! half-words -- the two BB rows are full words -- entry label I6225.
! PDF p.87 prints the routine title as "----1262---TEST EX AND EXIC."
! and says of this test: "-TEST 1 CHECKS THE EXECUTION OF / -ALL
! CLASSES OF INSTRUCTIONS / -AND THAT ILLEGAL EXECUTES WILL / -SET THE
! CORRECT INDICATORS."
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE, and that is not a slip.  jb_ax5b's LISTING pages
! carry no printed page numbers at all -- the "12 11 10 9" down the
! left margin is fanfold carriage-tape line numbering, and the only
! printed numbers are in the front write-up, which is scanned 2-up.
! Every verify_ax5b_*.py here already says "PDF p.NN" for that reason.
!
! WHERE THIS WAS CUT, AND WHY.  TEST 1CC runs 023460.40-023545.40, 105
! half-words over PDF pp.92-94 -- too long for one file.  The cut is at
! 023474.40, the label I6225, whose comment column reads "-DO BE AND
! BD."; PDF p.92's "BD,I6225" at 023473.00 is the branch that enters
! it, so the cut is on a real seam and not mid-stanza.  What is left
! behind on p.92 (023460.40-023474.00) is 1CC's FIRST subject class,
! EX of a BIND (branch-on-indicator) instruction, with its own four
! error entries I6221/16222/.../I6224.  What is taken is the second,
! third and fourth: BE, BD and BB.  The right-hand end, 023545.40, is
! the label I6240 -- the test's own exit, and the target of five
! branches inside the transcribed range; the rows after it on p.94
! ("BD,16218 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW -TO SSIP. / BD,$+.32" and the
! IC262 continuity update) are 1262's shared exit tail, not 1CC.
!
! THIS BLOCK IS THE SPECIFICATION FOR THE EXE INDICATOR.  Reference
! Manual printed p.49 (PDF p.52), on EXECUTE: "the subject instruction
! is not allowed to change the state of the interruption system or
! replace the contents of the instruction counter.  The execution
! exception indicator (EXE) is turned on by any branch operation of a
! subject instruction in which the condition for a successful branch is
! met.  When indicator EXE is actuated, the branch and all associated
! operations are not performed.  The suppressed actions include the
! disabling in BRANCH DISABLED, the enabling in BRANCH ENABLED or
! BRANCH ENABLED AND WAIT, the counting and refilling in COUNT, BRANCH
! AND REFILL, and so on."  The BE, BD and BB clauses of that paragraph
! are error entries on these two pages -- NOT every clause: no COUNT,
! BRANCH AND REFILL and no BRANCH ENABLED AND WAIT appears as an EX
! SUBJECT anywhere in 1CC (the CB+ rows here are the table-fill loop's
! own instructions, not subjects), so the counting-and-refilling
! suppression is stated by the manual and left unwitnessed by this
! block.  FOURTEEN error entries, not twelve -- I6238 and
! I6239 are easy to miss because their subject (I62B6) is the one whose
! branch condition is NOT met, so they read like near-duplicates of
! I6237.  Verbatim, in listing order:
!
!   023502.40  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BE
!              -INSTR EXECUTED, BRANCH NOT EXECUTED.
!   023504.00  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BE INSTR
!   (I6226)    -EXECUTED,BRANCH EXECUTED.
!   023507.00  -SYSTEM ENABLED AFTER EX OF
!   (I6228)    -A BE INSTRUCTION.
!   023515.00  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BD INSTR
!   (I6230)    -EXECUTED, BRANCH NOT EXECUTED.
!   023516.40  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BD INSTR
!   (I6231)    -EXECUTED, BRANCH EXECUTED.
!   023521.00  -SYSTEM DISABLED AFTER EX OF
!              -A BD INSTRUCTION.
!   023525.40  -BB BIT 0 FAILS, UNABLE TO EX SAME.
!              -TERM THIS TEST.
!   023530.40  -BB,BIT 1 IS 0, FAILS, UNABLE
!              -TO EXECUTE SAME, TERM THIS TEST.
!   023533.40  -NO INT WHEN EX BB,COND
!              -FOR BRANCH MET, BRANCH NOT TAKEN.
!   023535.00  -NO INT WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
!   (I6234)    -BRANCH MET, BRANCH TAKEN.
!   023536.40  -NO INT WHEN EX BB, COND FOR BRANCH
!   (I6235)    -MET, NO BRANCH, CONTROL GIVEN TO NEXT
!              -INSTRUCT FOLLOWING BRANCH.
!   023541.40  -INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
!   (I6237)    -BRANCH NOT MET, NO BRANCH.
!   023543.00  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
!   (I6238)    -BRANCH NOT MET, BRANCH TAKEN.
!   023544.40  -NO INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB,COND FOR
!   (I6239)    -BRANCH NOT MET, NO BRANCH, CONTROL
!              -GIVEN TO INSTR AFTER BB.
!
! The punctuation is transcribed, not tidied: I6226 prints
! "-EXECUTED,BRANCH EXECUTED." with no space after the comma while
! I6231 prints "-EXECUTED, BRANCH EXECUTED." with one; 023533.40 and
! I6239 print "BB,COND" while I6234/I6235/I6237/I6238 print "BB, COND".
! "-BB BIT 0 FAILS" has no comma after BB, "-BB,BIT 1 IS 0" has one.
!
! I6237 IS THE ONE WITH NO LEADING "NO", and that inversion is the
! whole point of the entry.  I6237's address is planted into the
! interrupt landing before "EX,I62B6" runs, so I6237 is reached ONLY
! by an interruption.  I62B6's subject is a branch whose condition is
! NOT met, so no successful branch occurred, so EXE must NOT come on,
! so no interruption must occur.  Arriving at I6237 at all IS the
! failure, and the message says so: "-INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB, COND FOR /
! -BRANCH NOT MET, NO BRANCH."  Every other entry in the block is
! reached by falling through or by a wrongly-taken branch, so every
! other message says "NO INT TAKEN".
!
! THE INTERRUPT VECTOR IS THE INSTRUMENT.  PDF p.109's constants area
! for 1262, read at 600 dpi in its own LABEL column, gives the three
! pieces:
!
!   I62K1  BD,I62ITE        24320.04 00     024172.00
!          BD,I62ITE        24320.04 00     024172.40
!   I62K6  B,I62ITE+.32     24320.50 00     024177.00
!          B,I62ITE+.32     24320.50 00     024177.40
!   I62INT DR%BU,64,8@,64   -INTRPT TABLE.  024220.00
!   I62ITE BD,$             24320.04 00     024320.00
!          B,$              24320.50 00     024320.40
!   I62XW1 XW,0,64,I62INT   0.00 00 002000.50 90   024326.00
!
! I62XW1's three fields, decoded against the XW rows on PDF pp.113-114
! rather than assumed from the operand order: VALUE 0 (the whole first
! half-word prints 0.00 00), COUNT 64 (the one set bit in "002000" is
! bit 39, and the count field is bits 28-45 -- p.114's "BIT28 XW,0,
! 131072,0" prints 0.00 08, putting 2**17 at bit 28), REFILL I62INT
! (bits 46-63 read 10384 = 0o24220; p.113's "I74K4 XW,0,0,I74K1" reads
! 10553 = 0o24471 in the same field).  So the loop's address walk
! starts from a value of ZERO and is stepped by CB+; the I62INT base
! comes from the SX instruction's own address field, and the refill
! field is never used here because CB+ has refill = 0.
!
! I62K1 and I62K6 are each a FULL WORD holding the same half-word
! branch twice, and I62ITE is a full word holding two self-loops -- a
! "BD,$" at 024320.00 and a "B,$" at 024320.40.  So the four-row stanza
!
!       LX,$X1,I62XW1  /  LX,$X2,I62Kn  /  SX,$X2,I62INT%$X1@
!                      /  CB+,$X1,$-.32
!
! is a LOOP that writes one constant into all 64 words of the
! interrupt table -- it is not a single write to I62ITE.  The table
! entry then branches to one HALF of the I62ITE pair, and which half
! it lands on is what the choice of constant decides:
!
!   I62K6 = B,I62ITE+.32   -> lands on 024320.40, and "B" leaves the
!                             interruption system as it found it
!   I62K1 = BD,I62ITE      -> lands on 024320.00, and "BD" enters the
!                             landing with the system DISABLED
!
! The test then plants its handler address in the matching half with
! "SVA,$X1,I62ITE+.32" or "SVA,$X1,I62ITE" -- SVA overwrites only the
! address part, so the landing keeps its own B or BD.  The pairing
! holds across the whole block without exception: I6225's loop loads
! I62K6 and every SVA up to 023520.00 says "I62ITE+.32"; I6233's loop
! reloads I62K1 and both SVAs after it (023532.40, 023540.00) say
! "I62ITE".  WHICH VECTOR FIRES is therefore how 1CC reads out whether
! a suppressed BE/BD left the enable state alone.
!
! AND THAT EXPLAINS THE "-ILLEGAL OP." ROW, which programs/ax5b_162_
! test3a.strap had to leave unexplained.  The word 00000003740 is an
! operation-code-invalid datum standing in the straight-line
! instruction path (023506.00 and 023520.40 here; 024144.40 and
! 024155.40 in TEST 3A).  It is a PROBE FOR THE ENABLE STATE: if the
! interruption system is enabled, executing it interrupts; if disabled,
! it does not.  Both uses here read out exactly that, in opposite
! directions, and the neighbouring error text is the proof:
!
!   I6227 (BE case).  The subject was "BE,I6226" -- BRANCH ENABLED, a
!   successful branch, so EXE must fire and the ENABLING must be
!   suppressed, leaving the system DISABLED.  The probe must therefore
!   NOT interrupt, and the correct path is to fall past it to
!   "BD,I6229".  An interruption goes to the planted I6228: "-SYSTEM
!   ENABLED AFTER EX OF / -A BE INSTRUCTION."
!
!   I6232 (BD case).  "BE,$+.32" at 023514.00 enables the system for
!   real first; the subject was "BD,I6231" -- BRANCH DISABLED, again a
!   successful branch, so the DISABLING must be suppressed and the
!   system must still be ENABLED.  The probe must therefore INTERRUPT,
!   to the planted I6233.  Falling past it is the failure: "-SYSTEM
!   DISABLED AFTER EX OF / -A BD INSTRUCTION."
!
! ONE ROW IS STILL NOT EXPLAINED BY THESE PAGES.  023510.00's
! "LX,$X1,I62XW1" carries the comment "-SETUP B,I62ITE+.32 INT TABLE",
! but the stanza has no store loop: the very next row, "LVI,$X1,I6232",
! overwrites the value I62XW1 just supplied, and the table still holds
! whatever I6225's loop put there -- which is indeed B,I62ITE+.32, so
! the COMMENT is true of the machine state while the LX that carries it
! does no work.  Stated rather than rationalised, in the manner of
! ax5b_16082_op_ad.strap's "NOT TRACED" block.  The ENCODING of the row
! is settled either way, and that is what this file checks.
!
! THE TWO BARE BB ROWS ARE A PRE-FLIGHT, not part of the EXE contract.
! 023524.00 "LX,$X0,BIT0" loads index register 0 with the word BIT0
! (PDF p.114's label column: "BIT0 XW,%8@400000.00,0,0" at 024522.00 --
! bit 0 set, every other bit clear).  023524.40's "BB,$X0,$+2.32" then
! proves a plain BB branches on that 1 bit and 023527.00's
! "BB,$X0+.01,$+1.32" proves it does not branch on the 0 bit beside it.
! If either fails the deck reports "UNABLE TO EX SAME" and branches to
! I6240, because a BB that does not work cannot be used as an EX
! subject.  Those same two bit addresses are what the EX subjects test:
! PDF p.109 gives "I62B5 BB,$X0,I6234" at 024204.00 (condition MET) and
! "I62B6 BB,$X0+.01,I6238" at 024205.40 (condition NOT met).
!
! WHY I62B6 SITS AT A .40 HALF-WORD, self-checked and not assumed:
! "EX,I62B6" at 023540.40 prints "24205.52 00", and octal pair 52 =
! 101010 has BIT 18 = 1, so the subject half-word is 024205.40.  PDF
! p.109 agrees: I62B5's "BB,$X0,I6234" is a FULL WORD occupying
! 024204.00-024204.40, its "B,I6235" takes 024205.00, and I62B6 starts
! at 024205.40.  Every other EX in 1CC prints pair 12 (bit 18 = 0).
!
! ENCODING ONLY, and it could not be otherwise: a run needs the 64-word
! interrupt table, the I62B* subject constants, SSIP's SEN/SERS
! reporting, I60S1's body, and an EX the model actually EXECUTES.  EX
! is in MISC_CODES, so the ASSEMBLER encodes it; that is the whole
! distinction.
!
! STILL ENCODING ONLY AS OF 2026-09-25, and the reason has changed.
! The model now EXECUTES EX, including this block's whole contract --
! the EXE indicator, the suppressed branch, the suppressed enabling in
! BRANCH ENABLED and disabling in BRANCH DISABLED, and control
! returning after the EXECUTE rather than after the subject.  What
! still keeps this file off the runnable list is everything ELSE in
! the first sentence: the interrupt table, SSIP, and I60S1.  The
! behavioural counterpart, written from the manual against this
! block's own clauses, is programs/ex_exe.strap, and this file is
! cited in its header as the deck oracle.
!
! WHAT IS NEW HERE FOR THIS ASSEMBLER, checked by grep and not
! asserted: nothing in the mnemonic list is a first.  BE is already
! witnessed by verify_ax1a_bew_listing.py and four jb_ax5b files, CB+
! by verify_ibox4_listing.py and verify_ax5b_160_test8b_listing.py, BB
! by verify_fp_arith_f206a_listing.py's "BB,ROS+.60,$+2.0" at
! 013574.40.  What this block adds is EX four times over -- more EX
! rows than the rest of the repo holds -- the first BB with an INDEX
! REGISTER as its bit operand ("$X0" and "$X0+.01", where f206a tests a
! core word), and the first row anywhere here whose EX subject sits at
! a .40 half-word (023540.40).
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_162_test1cc_listing.py.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: three, all spelling, none semantic -- and a fourth
! that has been retired.
!   1. RETIRED.  This item used to read "numeric labels prefixed L
!      (L16225...L16240, L162B3...L162B6, L162INT, L162ITE, L162K1,
!      L162K6, L162XW1, L160S1, L160SX1), as ax5b_162_exic_classes.
!      strap and ax5b_162_test3a.strap already do for 1262.  BIT0,
!      SEN and SERS need none."  None of those files prefixes now:
!      the leading glyph was measured at 600 dpi and it is the LETTER
!      I, so I6225...I6240, I62B3...I62B6, I62INT, I62ITE, I62K1,
!      I62K6, I62XW1, I60S1 and I60SX1 are legal STRAP-1 symbols as
!      the page prints them (docs/listing_typography.md).  BIT0, SEN
!      and SERS never needed anything and still do not.
!   2. The listing's "%...@" pair is this assembler's "(...)":
!      "I62INT%$X1@" is written "I62INT($X1)" and
!      "%8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740" is written "DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740".
!   3. The DD's datum keeps its "(8)" for the reason ax5b_162_test3a.
!      strap measured: this assembler's default radix is DECIMAL, so a
!      bare 3740 assembles as 00000007234.  The "(8)" is load-bearing.
!   4. Octal in SYN addresses is written "(8)".  Bit offsets inside
!      SOURCE fields are NOT converted -- "$+2.32", "$+1.32", "$-.32",
!      "$+2.0", "$+1.0", "I62ITE+.32", "$X0+.01" are copied verbatim,
!      because STRAP source bit offsets are decimal (32 bits = half a
!      word) even though the listing's LOCATION column prints bit
!      offsets in octal (".40" = 32).  ax5b_162_test3a.strap's
!      "$+1.32" already establishes this and passes.
! No CNOP appears in this range; 1262's CNOPs are all on PDF p.109.
!
! EXTERNALS, SYN'd at the addresses this same listing prints.  THESE
! ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES -- the same caveat
! verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about I6088.  A SYN row
! MAKES the address field come out right, so the rows naming one prove
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.  The
! block's genuine address evidence is elsewhere and there is a great
! deal of it: FIFTEEN labels defined inside the range (I6226 through
! I6240), sixteen rows whose operand is one of them, and EIGHT
! self-relative rows.  I6225 is NOT evidence -- the SLC above sets the
! counter to 023474.40 and I6225 is the first label after it, so
! checking it checks the SLC against the number this transcription fed
! the SLC.  It is asserted anyway, as the block's anchor.

I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0            ! 1260's SIC return link
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0            ! 1260's "CLR INDS 0-19" subroutine
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
I62INT SYN, (8)24220.0            ! the 64-word interrupt table, PDF p.109
I62ITE SYN, (8)24320.0            ! "-ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE.", p.109
I62K1  SYN, (8)24172.0            ! the word "BD,I62ITE", twice, p.109
I62K6  SYN, (8)24177.0            ! the word "B,I62ITE+.32", twice, p.109
I62XW1 SYN, (8)24326.0            ! "XW,0,64,I62INT" -- the fill loop's IW
I62B3  SYN, (8)24202.0            ! "BE,I6226 / B,I6227"   subject, p.109
I62B4  SYN, (8)24203.0            ! "BD,I6231 / B,I6232"   subject, p.109
I62B5  SYN, (8)24204.0            ! "BB,$X0,I6234 / B,I6235"       p.109
I62B6  SYN, (8)24205.40           ! "BB,$X0+.01,I6238 / B,I6239"   p.109
BIT0    SYN, (8)24522.0            ! the word with bit 0 set, PDF p.114
        SLC, (8)23474.40
!
! ---- BE: fill all 64 table entries with "B,I62ITE+.32" -------------
I6225  LX,  $X1, I62XW1          ! -DO BE AND BD.  value 0, count 64
        LX,  $X2, I62K6           ! the word "B,I62ITE+.32" twice
        SX,  $X2, I62INT($X1)     ! store it into one table entry
        CB+, $X1, $-.32            ! ...and round again, 64 times
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LVI, $X1, I6227           ! the handler for the BE case
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE+.32      ! planted in the half I62K6 lands on
        SIC, I60SX1
        BD,  I60S1                !   clear indicators 0-19
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        EX,  I62B3                ! THE TEST: EX of "BE,I6226"
        SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BE
        B,   SERS                  ! -INSTR EXECUTED, BRANCH NOT EXECUTED.
        BD,  I6227                ! resume after SERS reports
!
I6226  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BE INSTR
        B,   SERS                  ! -EXECUTED,BRANCH EXECUTED.
!
! ---- I6227: was the ENABLING suppressed?  probe with an illegal op --
I6227  LVI, $X1, I6228
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE+.32      ! the probe's handler
        DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740       ! -ILLEGAL OP CODE.  (see header)
        BD,  I6229                ! no interrupt: system still disabled
!
I6228  SIC, SEN                   ! -SYSTEM ENABLED AFTER EX OF
        BD,  SERS                  ! -A BE INSTRUCTION.
!
! ---- BD: the table is still "B,I62ITE+.32" (see header on this LX) --
I6229  LX,  $X1, I62XW1          ! -SETUP B,I62ITE+.32 INT TABLE
        LVI, $X1, I6232           ! the handler for the BD case
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE+.32
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1                !   clear indicators 0-19
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   3.0                   ! clear the boundary register
        BE,  $+.32                 ! ENABLE for real, so the suppressed
        EX,  I62B4                !   disabling has something to undo
        ! THE TEST: EX of "BD,I6231"
I6230  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BD INSTR
        B,   SERS                  ! -EXECUTED, BRANCH NOT EXECUTED.
        B,   I6232                ! resume after SERS reports
!
I6231  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN BD INSTR
        B,   SERS                  ! -EXECUTED, BRANCH EXECUTED.
!
! ---- I6232: was the DISABLING suppressed?  same probe, other way ----
I6232  LVI, $X1, I6233
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE+.32      ! the probe's handler
        DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740       ! -ILLEGAL OP CODE.  (see header)
        SIC, SEN                   ! -SYSTEM DISABLED AFTER EX OF
        BD,  SERS                  ! -A BD INSTRUCTION.
!
! ---- BB: refill all 64 entries with "BD,I62ITE" ---------------------
I6233  LX,  $X1, I62XW1          ! -DO BB, SETUP BD INT TBL.
        LX,  $X2, I62K1           ! the word "BD,I62ITE" twice
        SX,  $X2, I62INT($X1)
        CB+, $X1, $-.32            ! 64 times again
!
! ---- pre-flight: does a PLAIN BB work at all? -----------------------
        LX,  $X0, BIT0             ! $X0 := bit 0 set, all else clear
        BB,  $X0, $+2.32           ! bit 0 is 1 -> must branch
        SIC, SEN                   ! -BB BIT 0 FAILS, UNABLE TO EX SAME.
        B,   SERS                  ! -TERM THIS TEST.
        B,   I6240
!
        BB,  $X0+.01, $+1.32       ! bit 1 is 0 -> must NOT branch
        BD,  $+2.0                 ! the good path
        SIC, SEN                   ! -BB,BIT 1 IS 0, FAILS, UNABLE
        B,   SERS                  ! -TO EXECUTE SAME, TERM THIS TEST.
        B,   I6240
!
! ---- EX of a BB whose branch condition IS met -----------------------
        LVI, $X1, I6236
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE          ! now the BD half of the landing
        EX,  I62B5                ! THE TEST: EX of "BB,$X0,I6234"
        SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT WHEN EX BB,COND
        B,   SERS                  ! -FOR BRANCH MET, BRANCH NOT TAKEN.
        B,   I6236
!
I6234  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
        B,   SERS                  ! -BRANCH MET, BRANCH TAKEN.
        B,   I6236
!
I6235  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT WHEN EX BB, COND FOR BRANCH
        B,   SERS                  ! -MET, NO BRANCH, CONTROL GIVEN TO NEXT
                                   ! -INSTRUCT FOLLOWING BRANCH.
!
! ---- EX of a BB whose branch condition is NOT met -------------------
I6236  LVI, $X1, I6237
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE
        EX,  I62B6                ! THE TEST: EX of "BB,$X0+.01,I6238"
        B,   I6240                ! the ONLY correct outcome: fall on
!
I6237  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
        B,   SERS                  ! -BRANCH NOT MET, NO BRANCH.
        B,   I6240
!
I6238  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB, COND FOR
        B,   SERS                  ! -BRANCH NOT MET, BRANCH TAKEN.
        B,   I6240
!
I6239  SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INT TAKEN WHEN EX BB,COND FOR
        B,   SERS                  ! -BRANCH NOT MET, NO BRANCH, CONTROL
                                   ! -GIVEN TO INSTR AFTER BB.
!
I6240  B,   $+1.0                 ! 1CC's exit; the tail is on PDF p.94
        END, I6225
